module gunbc.key_relation_identity_wall

import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }

// Moved out of std.key_relation: a semantic reference into the v1 compiler cannot live in the
// std-core stage0 crate that keyed_roster depends on. The wall itself is still tracked at
// std.key_relation key_relation_identity_wall_next_rung_trigger.
// THE IDENTITY WALL'S FIRST COMPILER-SCALE CONSUMER, NAMED HERE BECAUSE THE WALL
// IS TRACKED HERE. DESIGN section 4b(2) obliges a class below its ceiling to name
// its next-rung trigger, and a trigger with no consumer is the untracked stall
// that clause forbids. That consumer is now identified: the compiler itself,
// where source text at a span is used as the identity key.
//
// WHY THIS ROW CARRIES NO MAGNITUDE, and it is a deliberate omission rather than
// an oversight. The two figures that made this consumer legible -- how many call
// sites key on authored text, and how many candidate errors the import deletion
// exposed in one build -- were measured once, on one tree, by an instrument that
// does not exist as an entry point. Under the 2026-08-24 operator ruling (name
// the instrument, never transcribe its output) a number no producer can
// re-derive is debt, not evidence, so the CONSUMER is named and the COUNTS are
// not. When an entry point re-derives them, it is cited here by symbol and the
// figures become legitimate unchanged.
data key_relation_identity_wall_first_consumer: DeclarationRef = decl_ref(module_path: "v1.std.core", decl_name: "authored_name_at")

// The identity key at this site is the AUTHORED SOURCE TEXT AT A SPAN, which is a content-derived
// key in exactly the sense key_relation_identity_wall_next_rung_trigger forbids: two declarations
// spelled the same are one key, and one declaration respelled is two. That is why the compiler is
// the wall's first consumer at scale rather than one more specimen -- the impostor separation the
// trigger describes (key_of returns SubjectKey only) is what would make this site stop compiling.
// The namespace cut is the program that surfaces it, and its receipt is carried as an open PR
// rather than a file in this tree, so it is deliberately not cited here: a path into a document
// that will never merge is a citation to nothing.
